A||N||12||Call||Fiero Question||||5||
Z||000000||Call||12-24-1999||12:37 PM||||I am planning on buying a Fiero in a few months and I was wondering, I am am about 6'2 and most of my length is in my legs, is there alot of room in Fieros and will I fit?Also, if anyone knows, what is the max height of a person that could fit in a Fiero?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||12-24-1999||12:51 PM||||I am 6'3" and fit very well into my Fiero. I would suggest trying one on for size before you buy it, but they have a lot more room than it would appear.||||reg||10
Z||000002||terryk||12-24-1999||05:11 PM||||I'm 6'4" and it is fine. The tunnel is suprisingly long. Head room is fine too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voyd||12-24-1999||05:24 PM||||yea im 6'3" and i thought id never fit but let me tell you when you get inside there is ALOT of room and leg room is absolutely no problem. my seat isnt even close to being all the way back.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||12-24-1999||08:28 PM||||6'3" and no problem....||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||12-24-1999||08:31 PM||||6'3" and Fiero Compatible.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||12-24-1999||08:38 PM||||Sounds like some Fiero "tall"  tales||||reg||1
Z||000007||dogtired||12-25-1999||03:58 AM||||Lets not talk about my tall tail.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But I am only 6 ft, Love the car, find headroom in a sunroof car better, than without. Cars witout sunroof are ok if the headliner isn't hanging down, other wise static elect likes to hold yourr hair up   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Not sure of your experience with small short cars, but there is definately a technique one must learn to get in and out.<BR>Lets see, YOU Fall in, and Roll out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Sufficient leg room, I even move the seat up a notch to properly floor the clutch?<BR>Good luck, go try several on for SIZE. I think you will be pleased.||||reg||6
Z||000008||geyser||12-26-1999||01:39 AM||||I am 6'5", leg inseam just over 34". I fit just fine. There is more leg room in the automatics due to absent clutch pedal. Also, I have a size 16 shoe so foot room was also a concern. Not many sports cars fit the clydsdales of the human species but the Fiero does. Buy one, you won't regret it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||12-26-1999||10:34 AM||||Geeze, with a size 16 shoe, you could almost press two pedals at once!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||07:33 PM||||Or activate the wipers when you shift gears!<P>Call--I'm about 6'2" and kinda wide and I fit fine.  I'm not the only one who isn't rail thin either.  You'd be surprised how roomy these things are.  My wife has a '98 Cavalier and she said that there's more leg room in my Fiero than in her car.  (Of course, she's right!)  Unless you're over 7' tall or weigh more than 500# you'll fit.  I know a guy who's 6'9 1/2" tall and weighs close to 350 and he drives his everyday.  (Of course, he's got 1 ton springs under his! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000011||XenoGen||12-26-1999||11:09 PM||||<BR> Hmm, with all you people talking abou tall Fiero drivers, I'm starting to get concerned. I'm shbort! Does that mean I'm going to have difficulty reaching the peddles?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Actyually, I'm driven a Fiero once and I didn't seem to have any trouble reaching the peddles, but then again I didn't really notice anything besides "Hey, Look everybody, I'm driving a Fiero!"<P>  But I still wonder if the peddles might seem a little too far for my tastes on longer drives becasue I'm not too tall or anything. (5'5") Not enough not to reach, but perhaps ajust far enough to be a little uncomfortable, I wonder?<P><BR>(Oh, I said that when I drove the Fiero I didn't have any difficulty... Actually, I did - When I got in, I started to turn the wheel to turn the car around, but it wouldn't move. I thought something was wrong.  I didn't know that the Fieros didn't have power steering!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Actually, I just assumed that like all cars past the 60's had power steering. So at first I couldn't figure out why the wheel was so hard to turn.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000012||dogtired||12-26-1999||11:48 PM||||XenoGen: Just make sure you keep your seat rails greased, ( I mean the ones in the car ) Its a real pain in the tush when shorter people get out and leave the seat up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I know a time or two, I almost tore my bolster (mine, not the cars) off when trying to get in after a height defecient person got out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>The seats have quite a lot of movement, & wouldn't be concerned unless you are under 4 ft tall  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
